                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5fbc8752-c99e-301c-99aa-47b822daebf2",
                        "entry_id": "4d9eb548-4672-3dd7-8642-2d8783f9cecd",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Genuine or authentic; hence of behaviour: correct, socially acceptable or proper."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3cc323c8-7e11-4cdc-988b-9069cb6e7c1d",
                                "sense_id": "5fbc8752-c99e-301c-99aa-47b822daebf2",
                                "text": "Maha Rajah said it was necessary to witness it to make it pukka; and they said so too, and then signed it."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2e5e1d40-c300-44fd-8aad-744560337745",
                                "sense_id": "5fbc8752-c99e-301c-99aa-47b822daebf2",
                                "text": "The measures which resulted in the crushing of the mutiny within the Five Rivers, were unquestionably pukka. […] Pukka and kucha statesmanship are, indeed, two things which time rarely fails to detect, just as it tries the durability of a public building or a bridge."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "789afdb2-8b42-4a33-abb0-6ce46ff04ade",
                                "sense_id": "5fbc8752-c99e-301c-99aa-47b822daebf2",
                                "text": "Mrs. S[mart].— […] Are you not aware, Fanny, that he [Lieut. Marsden] is only Acting-Assistant Sub-Deputy Inspector? Do you imagine that I should give my child to a man whose appointment was not pucka? / F[anny].—But, Mamma, is Mr. Cholmondeley's appointment pucka? / Mrs. S.—How can you talk such nonsense, child? […] Mr. Cholmondeley is a landed gentleman, and draws twelve thousand rupees a month from his estates in Derbyshire, besides holding Government paper to a large amount."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c9aa57e0-73ec-4236-8ac0-7608968283c5",
                                "sense_id": "5fbc8752-c99e-301c-99aa-47b822daebf2",
                                "text": "'No one else here?' he said. 'I thought we were going to have a pukka consultation with all the crowd present – decorations, banners, and salute of guns!'"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f96b935d-9f5c-45ae-b505-0461a9296424",
                                "sense_id": "5fbc8752-c99e-301c-99aa-47b822daebf2",
                                "text": "But let's assume it's a real pukka rare bird."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ca951230-b3d6-4ef5-a2b1-405dd9074dfc",
                                "sense_id": "5fbc8752-c99e-301c-99aa-47b822daebf2",
                                "text": "Among [Max] Le Blond's exhortations was the need for Singapore theatre to internalise \"the conviction that our lives as Singaporeans possess the same theatrical validity, […] [as] the English literary tradition\"[…]. This would involve ridding ourselves of a residual colonial consciousness, even at the subliminal level, and revising our perception of the vernacular idiom and local accents, hitherto regarded as non-pukka."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ac302ad5-7c61-346f-a083-288c5620dd1a",
                        "entry_id": "4d9eb548-4672-3dd7-8642-2d8783f9cecd",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Constructed as a permanent building, with high-quality materials (especially fired clay bricks and tiles as opposed to unfired mud and thatch)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "South-Asia"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "da854c0d-aee0-49f6-aac4-9a25dd064a39",
                                "sense_id": "ac302ad5-7c61-346f-a083-288c5620dd1a",
                                "text": "The popular classification of wells is, however, into pukka and kuchcha. Percolation wells are usually pukka or brickbuilt. Spring wells are of three kinds—(1) pukka, where the sub-soil to the spring is sandy, and masonry is necessary througout; […] (3) kuchcha wells, made of clay throughout."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "82a8495c-bf50-4b92-aa9e-51a942ffd4e6",
                                "sense_id": "ac302ad5-7c61-346f-a083-288c5620dd1a",
                                "text": "In some cases, the sericulturists avail of credit facility and construct a pukka shed for the silk worms. It is ironical, however, that they have to accommodate themselves and their children in a shabby hut."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1f3e6112-3ee7-4eb6-b6b5-111f2bfed885",
                                "sense_id": "ac302ad5-7c61-346f-a083-288c5620dd1a",
                                "text": "The kutcha house made of mud, bamboo, and thatch and its modern replacement the pukka house, constructed of fired bricks, cement, and steel."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1b12a39e-1027-3e63-b701-1ba891ba8f1d",
                        "entry_id": "4d9eb548-4672-3dd7-8642-2d8783f9cecd",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Superior or of high quality; first-class; excellent."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "British",
                            "slang"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "29879a25-899a-47ee-b6ae-a59768cb1ac9",
                                "sense_id": "1b12a39e-1027-3e63-b701-1ba891ba8f1d",
                                "text": "Mind you, it was a pukka, respectable opium-house, and not one of those stifling, sweltering chandoo-khanas, that you can find all over the City."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
